{"id": 22, "ts": 1780602607.2666638, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clarification on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s communication challenges \u2013 difficulty articulating ideas and an egocentric stance can indeed hinder the rapid, clear exchanges required in a long\u2011haul cockpit, even if he generally creates a positive atmosphere. Those concerns directly touch the crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication criteria we flagged as critical.\nComparing that with Candidate\u202fB, we have solid evidence of high operational reliability (very conscientious), strong stress resilience (handles stress very well), and technical competence (excellent computer skills and good weather\u2011assessment ability). While B is sometimes perceived as pretentious and may adopt the wrong tone, those issues appear less likely to obstruct essential information flow than C\u2019s documented difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric behavior, especially under high\u2011workload conditions.\nGiven that crew cooperation hinges on clear, concise communication, I remain convinced that B\u2019s strengths outweigh his communication style flaws, whereas C\u2019s communication deficits pose a more direct safety risk. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fB for the long\u2011distance pilot position."}
