{"id": 66, "ts": 1780602880.2443914, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s point that Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress\u2011handling record is solid, but I was still uneasy about the reports of grumpy or uncooperative behavior. After asking Emily for concrete examples, she confirmed there are no specific incidents documented\u2014only a general note that B can be pretentious and sometimes uses the wrong tone. Without evidence of a real impact on crew dynamics, that concern is less decisive.\nConversely, Candidate\u202fC still lacks any concrete observation of calmness under high\u2011pressure or crisis situations; we only know he makes quick, correct decisions and is 100\u202f% reliable. Reliability and a positive crew atmosphere are essential, yet they do not guarantee the stress resilience needed for long\u2011haul flights. Moreover, his egocentric attitude and communication difficulties could become safety\u2011relevant when stress spikes.\nGiven that B demonstrably handles stress well, possesses strong technical skills (weather assessment, computer proficiency), and we have no proven negative effect on crew cooperation, I now believe B offers the more balanced fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
