{"id": 70, "ts": 1780602927.9370766, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s solid stress handling and technical skills, and Emily\u2019s confirmation that there are no documented incidents of crew\u2011disruptive behavior. However, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit. We have explicit evidence that C \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d which directly addresses the stress\u2011resilience criterion essential for long\u2011haul flights. Moreover, C is \u201c100\u202f% reliable\u201d and \u201ccreates a positive crew atmosphere,\u201d covering both operational reliability and crew cooperation\u2014two of our highest\u2011priority criteria. While C does have communication challenges and an egocentric attitude, those concerns are outweighed by the concrete proof of calmness under pressure and flawless reliability. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s \u201cweak memory for numbers\u201d poses a tangible safety risk in calculations, and his \u201cpretentious\u201d tone, although not yet linked to a specific incident, remains a potential crew\u2011cooperation issue. Given the decisive evidence of C\u2019s calmness and reliability, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC."}
