{"id": 74, "ts": 1780602964.1798182, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I respect James\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s calmness in a crisis and flawless reliability, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall fit for our long\u2011haul role.\u202fB\u2019s record shows very strong stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d) and solid technical competence \u2013 he assesses weather conditions accurately and has excellent computer skills, which are critical for complex international flights.\u202fHis conscientious nature further supports operational reliability.\u202fWhile James points to C\u2019s calmness, C also has documented communication difficulties, an egocentric attitude, and a reluctance to pursue further education, all of which raise concerns about crew cooperation, professional communication, and adaptability \u2013 criteria that are equally vital for long\u2011distance operations.\u202fIn contrast, B\u2019s pretentious tone and occasional wrong\u2011tone incidents have not been linked to any safety\u2011relevant outcomes, and his numeric\u2011memory weakness remains unquantified.\u202fGiven the balance of proven strengths versus potential crew\u2011impact risks, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fB."}
