{"id": 95, "ts": 1780603065.5611658, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I acknowledge James\u2019s point that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s flawless reliability and calmness in a crisis are valuable, but I remain unconvinced that these strengths outweigh the concerns we have about his crew\u2011interaction profile.\u202fC is described as having difficulty communicating ideas, being regarded as egocentric, and showing little willingness to pursue further education. Even without a documented incident, those traits raise red flags for long\u2011haul operations where continuous feedback, crew coordination, and adaptability are essential. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrably handles stress well, is very conscientious, and brings strong technical capabilities\u2014accurate weather assessment and excellent computer skills\u2014that directly support safe international flights. Moreover, we have no concrete evidence that B\u2019s occasional grumpiness, pretentious tone, or weak numeric\u2011memory has ever compromised safety or crew cooperation. Given the balance of proven technical competence, stress resilience, and the absence of safety\u2011relevant incidents, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fB as the best overall fit."}
